      "side": 1,
      "message": "Ah sorry I didn\u0027t see that message. These are generated from webgpu.idl and the https://source.chromium.org/chromium/chromium/src/+/main:third_party/dawn/src/dawn/node/interop/\n\nThe getMappedRange comes from this part of the webgpu idl: https://github.com/gpuweb/gpuweb/blob/f177043de0977d71603dacb3e3b6a3e17abe3d46/webgpu.idl#L180 but we can\u0027t really modify the IDL.\n\nBasically it seems that we want a pointer to `this` as a JS object so that we can set it on a private symbol on the array buffer. We can modify the templates to have a ::CreateWithWeakThis that somehow passes the Napi::Object as the second argument of the constructor, or inject it a posteriori in GPUDevice::createBuffer.\n\nAlso can we have the symbols declared in a new file that will have versions for each env, similar to Wrapper::For in the templates? We are going to have more symbols in the future.",
